load_lora: only ship the "default" adapter tensors to vLLM.

With TRL >= 1.8 and beta != 0 (unsloth's generated GRPOConfig defaults to
beta=0.001), TRL adds a frozen copy of the LoRA adapter named "ref" to the
PEFT model and computes reference log-probs with it. load_lora() collected
EVERY lora_A/lora_B tensor from model.state_dict() and only stripped the
".default" infix, so reference-adapter keys were passed through verbatim
and vLLM failed on the first generation:

    ValueError: base_model.model.model.layers.0.self_attn.qkv_proj.
    lora_A.ref.weight is unsupported LoRA weight

(from parse_fine_tuned_lora_name in vllm/lora/utils.py). Only reproduces
when the vLLM engine has LoRA enabled (fast_inference + max_lora_rank);
the merged-weight sync path is unaffected.

Filter the state dict to the active "default" adapter.
--- a/unsloth_zoo/vllm_utils.py	2026-07-06 20:27:09.900980801 +0200
+++ b/unsloth_zoo/vllm_utils.py	2026-07-06 20:27:09.918348832 +0200
@@ -2939,7 +2939,12 @@
         peft_config = get_peft_config(save_directory)
         state_dict = model.state_dict()
         items = state_dict.items()
-        state_dict = {k.replace(".default", ""):v for k, v in items if ".lora_A." in k or ".lora_B." in k}
+        # Only ship the active "default" adapter to vLLM. TRL (beta != 0)
+        # adds a frozen reference adapter named "ref" for the KL term;
+        # its keys (e.g. ...lora_A.ref.weight) survive the .default strip
+        # and vLLM's parse_fine_tuned_lora_name() raises
+        # "... is unsupported LoRA weight".
+        state_dict = {k.replace(".default", ""):v for k, v in items if ".lora_A.default." in k or ".lora_B.default." in k}
 
         # vllm_lora_already_loaded(model)
         lora_request = LoRARequest(str(lora_request_id), lora_request_id, lora_tensors = state_dict, lora_config = peft_config)
